{"Metric tag keys for shard(s) are inconsistent across timers - 'produce' uses tags={\"shard\": shard_tag} while 'wait_produce' uses tags={\"shards\": shard_tag}. Should standardize on a single tag name across all shard-related metrics (produce, wait_produce, segment_size_bytes, flusher_unhealthy)": 0.8479974865913391, "The added time.sleep(0.1) is a no-op because time.sleep is monkeypatched to lambda _: None earlier in the test, so it won't actually wait and doesn't help the flusher progress": 0.7678954601287842, "Processes that haven't been waited on yet may never be terminated if the join deadline is exceeded early - when deadline expires the code breaks out of the for loop and skips remaining entries in self.processes, so their terminate() is never called": 0.9804423451423645, "When creating per-process SpansBuffer instances in _create_process_for_shards, only shards is passed, so if SpansBuffer relies on other configuration/state from the original buffer (e.g. Redis client, keys, limits), those settings are not preserved": 0.5361950397491455, "In _ensure_processes_alive, the restart logic treats both processes and threads uniformly (checking exitcode, calling kill, etc.), but threads don't support those semantics - should branch explicitly on process vs. thread": 0.564018726348877}